What are some possible ways to optimize the performance of a Ruby program that prints numbers from 1 to 50, using Scala code? Here is the current implementation in Ruby:
[ Ruby code ]
for i in 1..50
  puts i
end
And here is a possible solution in Scala:
// Using a for loop
for (i <- 1 to 50) {
  println(i)
}
// Using a while loop
var i = 1
while (i <= 50) {
  println(i)
  i += 1
}
// Using a tail-recursive function
def printNumbers(n: Int): Unit = {
  if (n > 0) {
    printNumbers(n - 1)
    println(n)
  }
}
printNumbers(50)

