import java.util.Arrays;
public class MedianCalculator {
    public static double calculateMedian(double[] numbers) {
        int length = numbers.length;
        Arrays.sort(numbers);

        if (length % 2 == 0) {
            int middleIndex = length / 2;
            return (numbers[middleIndex - 1] + numbers[middleIndex]) / 2.0;
        } else {
            int middleIndex = length / 2;
            return numbers[middleIndex];
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses the `Arrays.sort()` method to sort the array in O(n log n) time complexity. It then checks whether the length of the array is odd or even and calculates the median accordingly.
