In the main method, we call the add method and pass in the values 5 and 3 as arguments. These values are assigned to the parameters num1 and num2 within the add method. The method then calculates the sum of the two numbers and returns the result.
Finally, we assign the result of the add method to a variable called result and print out the value using System.out.println.
This example demonstrates how arguments can be used to pass values to a method and how those values can be used to perform a specific action within the method. It also shows how the return value of a method can be assigned to a variable and used in other parts of the program.

